---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro'; import { resources,gaps,sources,text } from '../lib/data'; import { withBase } from '../lib/paths';
const featured=resources.slice(0,6); const reviewed=resources.filter((r:any)=>['reviewed','deep_review'].includes(r.review_level)).length; const demoCount=resources.filter((r:any)=>r.demo).length;
---
<Base title="Islamic Tech Guide — v0.1"><section class="hero"><div class="hero-card"><div class="eyebrow">Islamic technology ecosystem</div><h1>Map what exists.<br/>See what is missing.</h1><p>An open archive for Islamic technology projects, tools and services — with progressive review, evidence, and editorial gap analysis designed to help the community direct effort more effectively.</p><p class="arabic-copy" dir="rtl">أرشيف مفتوح للمشاريع والأدوات والخدمات التقنية، مع تقييم تدريجي ورصد للفجوات لتوجيه الجهد إلى الأماكن الأكثر احتياجًا.</p><div class="meta"><span class="tag accent">Developer-first</span><span class="tag">Useful to end users</span><span class="tag">Static · Open Source</span><span class="tag">English-first</span></div></div><aside class="stats panel"><div class="stat"><strong>{resources.length}</strong><span>resource records</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{reviewed}</strong><span>reviewed / deep-reviewed</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{gaps.length}</strong><span>gap records</span></div><div class="stat"><strong>{sources.length}</strong><span>discovery sources</span></div></aside></section>
<div class="notice"><strong>UX test mode:</strong> {demoCount} synthetic resources intentionally use the same production-shaped model as real entries. They are marked <code>demo: true</code>.</div>
<div class="section-head"><div><h2>Explore the archive</h2><p>The same Resource records can be shown as cards, a compact table, or full detail pages.</p></div><a class="text-link" href={withBase('/resources/')}>Browse resources →</a></div><div class="grid">{featured.map((r:any)=><a class="card-link" href={withBase(`/resources/${r.id}/`)}><article class="card"><div class="meta"><span class="tag accent">{r.resource_type}</span><span class="tag">{r.review_level}</span>{r.demo&&<span class="tag demo">DEMO</span>}</div><h3>{r.name}</h3><p>{text(r.summary)}</p><div class="meta">{(r.domains||[]).slice(0,3).map((x:string)=><span class="tag">{x}</span>)}</div></article></a>)}</div>
<div class="split-cta"><article class="panel callout"><div class="eyebrow">Gap analysis</div><h2>Gaps are first-class records</h2><p>Problem, existing solutions, what is missing, impact, difficulty, volunteer fit, confidence and evidence.</p><a class="button" href={withBase('/gaps/')}>Browse gaps</a></article><article class="panel callout"><div class="eyebrow">Discovery provenance</div><h2>Aggregators are sources, not resources</h2><p>Collected repositories and lists are tracked separately with processing state and dates.</p><a class="button secondary" href={withBase('/sources/')}>View source registry</a></article></div></Base>
